62a8-56b3-bab6-7c4ff9bd30f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-2360" :question/problem "The velocity $v$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of a particle at time $t$ (in seconds) is given by $v(t)=3{t}^{2}-24t+45.$ Calculate the velocity of the particle when the acceleration $a$ is equal to $0\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-24t+45) \\\\  & =6t-24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=0,$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =6t-24 \\\\ 6t & =24 \\\\ t & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, to calculate the velocity at time $t=4,$ we substitute this into the equation for the velocity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(4) & =3(4)^{2}-24(4)+45 \\\\  & =48-96+45 \\\\  & =-3\\text{ m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity when $a=0\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ is $-3\\,\\text{m/s}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-2360/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0cdcbc5-c10b-5dd1-af9a-410d2d44a4c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-2360"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336419/field-1/c83dad47966289f2b630fa17126be120ac8106addc5fe86136c3a26880796b1f" :answer/id #uuid "510fda73-d45a-52f1-95b0-533e0f771ede" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{t+1}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336419/field-1/371a94755fbd28dc600ad0b51436331c25243f27c11000f948e571f8786d9226" :answer/id #uuid "f0a5c361-764b-5a8c-b304-f1074da136cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{t+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336419/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4bae2bb8-441a-5bb0-b5ae-2f2f77731b65" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336419/field-1/c83dad47966289f2b630fa17126be120ac8106addc5fe86136c