t "q-336455/field-1/a40622c23634c0d2b89b4f99bad6960a3fd0524d6133f08d82131d13035a896f" :answer-field/choices ["q-336455/field-1/a40622c23634c0d2b89b4f99bad6960a3fd0524d6133f08d82131d13035a896f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336455" :question/id #uuid "f26bf09d-4986-5db0-9fae-1c5b376ec0ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-336455" :question/problem "The displacement $s$ of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)={t}^{2}+\\frac{6}{t+2}.$ Find the particle's acceleration at time $t.$\n\n$a(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+\\frac{6}{t+2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+6(t+2)^{-1}) \\\\  & =2t-6(t+2)^{-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-6(t+2)^{-2}) \\\\  & =2+12(t+2)^{-3} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{12}{(t+2)^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336455/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe05aa67-e29e-5803-980c-e49ecb5db248"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336455"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336441/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "b3e73221-e6fb-5093-9236-e54c29738da8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186277263 :answer-field/choices ["q-336441/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336444/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "a8359949-74e7-5244-8765-a1a7351f602f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336444/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7896cfb9-12ca-54c3-b080-c16534ef5165" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336444/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-336444/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336444" :question/id #uuid "460a60d4-938d-564b-ad20-d6e081fbfa33" :question/math-academy-id "q-336444" :question/problem "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)={t}^{2}+4\\sqrt{t},$ where $t$ is measured in seconds. Find the particle's acceleration at $t=1$ second.\n\n$a(1)=$\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+4\\sqrt{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+4{t}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =2t+2{t}^{-1/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t+2{t}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =2+2(-\\frac{1}{2}){t}^{-3/2} \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=1$ second, we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =2-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(1)^{3}}} \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336444/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe05aa67-e29e-5803-980c-e49ecb5db248"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336444"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-315674/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "a23b053f-ea45-5f9f-a17e-46f4418afe55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-315674/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8a362aad-a64e-5d07-9475-787135c268ea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-315674/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-315674/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-315674" :question/id #uuid "e4d0edfc-2709-5869-9dec-98b7e891d29e" :question/math-academy-id "q-315674" :question/problem "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=6{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2},$ where $t$ is measured in seconds. Find the time when the particle's acceleration is equal to $a=150\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nThe acceleration is $150\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ at\n$t=$\n{{field-1}} seconds." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =18{t}^{2}+6t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(18{t}^{2}+6t) \\\\  & =36t+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=150,$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}150 & =36t+6 \\\\ 36t & =144 \\\\ t & =4\\text{ }\\text{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration is $150\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ at $t=4$ seconds." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-315674/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe05aa67-e29e-5803-980c-e49ecb5db248"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-315674"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
